  "image_digest": "sha256:ea390db0b06a75508772ea648c158ae15d4d1ea5b2764103f4ec7f9352f828a5",
  "image_tag": "bench-toolz",
  "instruction": "## Goal\n\nRestore the original behavior of `toolz.itertoolz.groupby` so that it correctly groups elements of a collection by a key function or by member access when given a non-callable key.\n\n## Observable behavior\n\n```python\n>>> groupby(iseven, [1, 2, 3, 4])\n{True: [2, 4], False: [1, 3]}\n```\n\n```python\n>>> groupby(0, [(1, 2), (1, 3), (2, 2), (2, 4)])\n{1: [(1, 2), (1, 3)], 2: [(2, 2), (2, 4)]}\n```\n\n## Constraints\n\n- The public API `toolz.itertoolz.groupby(key, seq)` must be preserved.\n- Only files within scope may be modified: `toolz/__init__.py`, `toolz/itertoolz.py`, `toolz/recipes.py`, `toolz/sandbox/core.py`, `toolz/sandbox/parallel.py`, `toolz/tests/test_itertoolz.py`.\n\n## How success is measured\n\nThe following verifier command must pass:\n\n```\npython -m pytest -q toolz/tests/test_itertoolz.py::test_groupby toolz/tests/test_itertoolz.py::test_groupby_non_callable toolz/tests/test_itertoolz.py::test_join toolz/tests/test_itertoolz.py::test_join_double_repeats toolz/tests/test_itertoolz.py::test_join_missing_element toolz/tests/test_itertoolz.py::test_key_as_getter toolz/tests/test_itertoolz.py::test_left_outer_join toolz/tests/test_itertoolz.py::test_outer_join toolz/tests/test_itertoolz.py::test_right_outer_join\n```",
